My Big Sister</b>

03:34.980 --> 03:37.870
<b>Episode 8</b>

03:34.980 --> 03:37.870
<b>I Can't 
Raise 
My Sword 
Against a Girl</b>

03:41.740 --> 03:44.950
Oh, come on now, Asahi. 
How long are you going to mope?

03:44.950 --> 03:46.820
Light Magic: Level 1...

03:46.820 --> 03:48.240
It sucks!

03:48.240 --> 03:50.820
A-Asahi, there's no need to be so down.

03:50.820 --> 03:54.460
Creating light yourself isn't
 something that's easy to do!

03:54.810 --> 04:00.170
That's right. It might not be useful in battle, 
but not needing a lantern is nice.

04:00.170 --> 04:05.090
It'll reduce our expenses.
Every home will want one of you! Yup!

04:05.090 --> 04:08.580
Thanks for the kind words, but could you
 not make me sound like an appliance?

04:10.030 --> 04:12.810
This place seems a bit dingy, doesn't it?

04:12.810 --> 04:15.280
Is this the quest location?

04:15.280 --> 04:19.820
Yeah. It's a criminal clan's hideout.
 The quest is to clear it out.

04:19.820 --> 04:20.820
If I recall...

04:21.070 --> 04:25.700
<b>Dark Crisis</b>

04:21.070 --> 04:25.700
<b>Dark Crisis</b>

04:21.090 --> 04:23.770
They call themselves Dark Crisis, right?

04:24.290 --> 04:26.070
Somebody's got crazy taste in names.

04:26.070 --> 04:28.950
Sorry for the craziness.

04:30.160 --> 04:33.120
Hey, kid. What business 
do you have at our base?

04:33.120 --> 04:36.480
Get lost or we'll beat you 
and drive you outta here.

04:36.960 --> 04:38.610
Oh, um, it's just...

04:43.430 --> 04:45.140
Whoa.

04:47.430 --> 04:49.390
Don't try to scare Asahi.

04:49.390 --> 04:52.770
We don't mind dragging both of you
around town, if that's what you want.

04:52.770 --> 04:54.950
Stop! Stop!

04:55.440 --> 04:58.520
Both of you, try to remember 
our <i>true</i> objective here.

04:59.330 --> 05:02.220
There are criminal clans that 
misuse the adventurer system.

05:02.220 --> 05:05.950
We want you to take down 
one of these clans, Asahi-kun.

05:05.950 --> 05:07.460
A <i>criminal</i> clan?!

05:08.330 --> 05:09.900
Such a thing exists?

05:09.900 --> 05:10.580
Yup.

05:10.620 --> 05:11.450
<b>Bad Guy</b>

05:11.080 --> 05:14.810
They forge adventurer rank
 badges, then sell them.

05:11.450 --> 05:12.700
<b>Bad Guy</b>

05:12.700 --> 05:13.450
<b>Bad Guy</b>

05:12.700 --> 05:13.450
<b>Adventurer</b>

05:13.450 --> 05:14.960
<b>Bad Guy</b>

05:13.450 --> 05:14.960
<b>Adventurer</b>

05:14.810 --> 05:16.750
They're a thorn in the side of the Guild!

05:14.960 --> 05:16.750
<b>Bad Guy</b>

05:14.960 --> 05:16.750
<b>Adventurer</b>

05:14.960 --> 05:16.750
<b>Money</b>

05:14.960 --> 05:16.750
<b>Money</b>

05:17.320 --> 05:22.250
At any rate, they're a bunch of criminals 
who debase the adventuring vocation.

05:22.250 --> 05:24.090
There are people like that, huh?

05:24.090 --> 05:27.870
Adventurer ranks are like ID
authorized by the royal capital!

05:27.870 --> 05:31.150
Anyone who'd falsify that is 
a disgrace to all adventurers!

05:28.760 --> 05:28.890
<b>Falsify</b>

05:28.890 --> 05:31.510
<b>Falsify</b>

05:31.150 --> 05:32.470
They're seriously scum!

05:31.260 --> 05:31.390
<b>Scum</b>

05:31.510 --> 05:32.140
<b>Falsify</b>

05:31.510 --> 05:32.140
<b>Scum</b>

05:32.140 --> 05:32.510
<b>Falsify</b>

05:32.140 --> 05:32.560
<b>Scum</b>

05:32.510 --> 05:37.140
<b>Falsify</b>

05:32.560 --> 05:37.140
<b>Scum</b>

05:32.800 --> 05:37.140
Y-Yeah, you're right. 
Falsifying your rank is totally wrong.

05:37.490 --> 05:40.660
This quest was posted
by the House of Brigandine.

05:40.660 --> 05:43.980
They're a noble family that gives 
their backing to Guild operations.

05:43.980 --> 05:46.490
Huh. So they're like patrons?

05:46.490 --> 05:51.320
Yeah. That's why widespread fake ranks 
are a problem for the nobles, too.

05:51.320 --> 05:54.130
I see. So who's my target?

05:54.130 --> 05:56.660
We'd like you to take care of Dark Crisis.

05:56.910 --> 06:00.920
<b>Dark Crisis</b>

05:56.910 --> 06:00.920
<b>Dark Crisis</b>

06:00.260 --> 06:02.890
There's another one called Overdose,

06:01.170 --> 06:03.670
<b>Overdose</b>

06:01.170 --> 06:03.670
<b>Overdose</b>

06:03.970 --> 06:06.920
but a different party's
 taking care of that one,

06:06.920 --> 06:09.930
so for now, could you 
handle this one, Asahi-kun?

06:10.670 --> 06:12.010
You got it!

06:12.970 --> 06:16.300
That's the sequence of events 
that led us here, but...

06:16.300 --> 06:16.890
Hey!

06:16.890 --> 06:18.640
You did the job during the flashback!

06:18.640 --> 06:19.550
It was simple.

06:19.550 --> 06:21.530
Didn't even count as a warm-up.

06:21.530 --> 06:25.730
You two can take out a gang of 
human thugs in an instant, huh?

06:25.730 --> 06:28.070
Wh-Wh-Wh-Who are you people?!

06:28.070 --> 06:30.160
The Guild sent you, didn't they?

06:30.160 --> 06:34.830
I am Ikusaba Asahi. And you're Lombert,
Dark Crisis' leader, aren't you?

06:34.830 --> 06:39.280
Asahi? The kid who rose to 
Ogre Class in just a month?

06:39.280 --> 06:41.970
But I'm Ogre Class, too!

06:41.970 --> 06:44.890
I'm the man known as 
Lightning Strike Lombert!

06:44.890 --> 06:46.760
I won't go down quietly!

06:54.120 --> 06:57.980
You're Ogre Class, but all you do is
commit crimes? Pathetic.

06:59.340 --> 07:01.130
You have real skills, don't you?

07:01.130 --> 07:03.360
Instead of committing crimes in the shadows,

07:03.360 --> 07:05.940
why don't you do something to help people?

07:07.680 --> 07:11.440
The Guild always hogs all the profits, 
and you're nothing more than its dog.

07:11.440 --> 07:13.370
You have no right to say anything!

07:13.900 --> 07:16.830
Enchant Thunder!

07:19.840 --> 07:23.040
<i>I'd expect no less from the 
leader of a criminal clan.</i>

07:23.390 --> 07:24.080
<i>But...</i>

07:24.800 --> 07:27.290
Today, you've encountered 
the wrong opponents.

07:30.990 --> 07:32.630
Exalted Hero!

07:32.630 --> 07:36.580
The sugary voice that always sounds like
it's bringing trouble in its wake...

07:38.000 --> 07:40.190
Sophie, reporting for support duty!

07:40.190 --> 07:42.190
Tanya-san told me you were here.

07:42.890 --> 07:45.520
Why couldn't Tanya keep her mouth shut?!

07:45.900 --> 07:50.210
Many wished to see the valiant Hero 
in action, so I brought a crowd with me!

07:50.210 --> 07:52.580
<i>And Sophie made it worse!</i>

07:54.390 --> 07:58.060
<i>With everyone watching, 
I can't have Maya-nee fight.</i>

07:58.060 --> 07:59.490
<i>Which means...</i>

08:00.300 --> 08:02.920
<i>I have to fight him?!</i>

08:04.450 --> 08:06.090
Thunderclap!

08:07.940 --> 08:10.800
<i>S-So this is the true ability
 of an Ogre Class adventurer?</i>

08:11.960 --> 08:13.510
I won't miss next time.

08:13.510 --> 08:16.220
I'll make sure you have 
no hope of recovering!

08:18.810 --> 08:19.990
M-My sword!

08:19.990 --> 08:22.890
This can't be! Did I exceed its
weapon durability?

08:35.410 --> 08:36.820
Wow! He beat him!

08:36.450 --> 08:39.160
So that's what the fabled
 Asahi-kun can really do!

08:43.320 --> 08:45.670
Maya-nee, nice assist.

08:46.830 --> 08:50.090
You're amazing! 
You really hung in there, Asahi!

08:50.320 --> 08:52.840
Okay, time for your reward.

08:52.840 --> 08:55.260
A hug from your big sister.

08:55.780 --> 08:58.900
Not while everyone's watching!

08:58.900 --> 09:00.470
Ow, ow, ow!

08:59.120 --> 09:00.470
Aw, come on.

09:01.090 --> 09:07.100
If they were this weak, the other clan's
probably not that strong either.

09:13.800 --> 09:15.220
D-Don't come any closer!

09:15.220 --> 09:17.700
I ain't lettin' you cause any more chaos!

09:18.870 --> 09:20.170
Stone Lightning Blossom...

09:20.830 --> 09:21.950
Six Strikes.

09:34.290 --> 09:35.460
You...

09:35.460 --> 09:39.810
The head of Overdose, 
the Bludgeoning Baron, Popinski.

09:41.390 --> 09:43.820
Troublesome flies must 
be dealt with like <i>this</i>!

09:49.610 --> 09:52.400
We thank you for the violent introduction.

09:52.700 --> 09:54.650
As a member of the House of Brigandine,

09:54.880 --> 09:57.490
giving you my name as well
 would only be polite, yes?

09:58.060 --> 10:00.240
My name is Gloria.

10:00.870 --> 10:05.500
I will engrave your name 
on Overdose's tombstone!

10:09.460 --> 10:11.670
Graceful Strike!

10:09.630 --> 10:12.380
<b>Graceful</b>

10:09.630 --> 10:12.380
<b>Graceful</b>

10:09.630 --> 10:12.380
<b>Graceful</b>

10:10.630 --> 10:12.380
<b>Strike</b>

10:10.630 --> 10:12.380
<b>Strike</b>

10:10.630 --> 10:12.380
<b>Strike</b>

10:16.840 --> 10:19.430
She took down our 
Ogre Class leader in one hit!

10:19.430 --> 10:22.300
I will take care of you all at once.

10:22.570 --> 10:24.630
Now, prepare yourselves.

10:24.630 --> 10:27.810
S-Someone help us!

10:27.810 --> 10:30.160
Musclebrains.

10:32.060 --> 10:35.310
Doing something as foolish 
as misusing their ranks...

10:35.850 --> 10:38.910
The caliber of adventurers 
certainly has fallen of late.

10:39.550 --> 10:42.070
Thank you for protecting me.

10:42.760 --> 10:47.170
Think nothing of it. Protecting their 
servants is one of a master's duties.

10:48.860 --> 10:52.830
Incidentally, Kuon, who is handling 
the other elimination mission?

10:53.150 --> 10:55.650
A boy by the name of Ikusaba Asahi.

10:57.160 --> 11:01.050
The prodigy who rose up the
 ranks even faster than me?

11:01.050 --> 11:04.470
Very suspicious. He reeks of wrongdoing.

11:07.300 --> 11:12.990
Only by crossing swords with him can 
the authenticity of his skills be verified.

11:12.990 --> 11:15.820
And I, Gloria Brigandine, shall do just that.

